# Shared edge proxy for the WHOLE VPS — the only binder of ports 80/443, shared by every
# project on the box (cosimosi, postpilot, whatever comes third). Lives at /srv/edge,
# managed by hand: edit → validate → `docker compose up -d`. It is NOT part of any
# project's deploy workflow; api stacks roll independently underneath it.
#
# This file is a router, not a config. Every site block lives in its own
# conf.d/<project>.caddy fragment, so adding the third and fourth project is "drop one
# file, append one line" instead of a merge conflict in a file everyone shares.
#
# Ownership contract (DEPLOY.md §4):
#   Caddyfile, docker-compose.yml  → the box, not a project. Do not edit them per project.
#   conf.d/<project>*.caddy        → that project alone owns its own files.
#   .env                           → append your PREFIXED domain vars; touch no one else's.
#
# Caddy config is all-or-nothing: one broken fragment takes down TLS for EVERY project on
# the box, not just its own. So always validate the assembled config before reloading:
#
#   docker run --rm -v /srv/edge/Caddyfile:/etc/caddy/Caddyfile:ro \
#     -v /srv/edge/conf.d:/etc/caddy/conf.d:ro --env-file /srv/edge/.env \
#     caddy:2-alpine caddy validate --config /etc/caddy/Caddyfile --adapter caddyfile
#
# Global options (ACME email, etc.) would go here and must be the FIRST block, before the
# import — that is the one reason to edit this file:
# {
# 	email ops@example.com
# }

# Relative to this file, i.e. /etc/caddy/conf.d/ in the container. Alphabetical order,
# which is irrelevant: distinct site addresses are order-independent.
import conf.d/*.caddy
